The personalities are published before the lockdown

Run 570's panel said d5: the candidates were turned away by the passive
match, the one that asks whether the nub is the thing the personality
wants.  The two candidates were the donor's -- AppleRMFabricTrace and
AppleARMLightEnLp -- and the name they wanted was cpurdebug-interface
against a nub called options-common.  That is what the donor's
personalities ask for, and it is not what this board is.

Our own personalities were not among the candidates at all, and that is the
whole of it: they were published into the catalogue too late.

There are two matching sweeps.  PE_lockdown_iokit() runs during the
lockdown, before bsd_init(), and this board's matching thread runs it.
StartIOKitMatching() runs after the lockdown, from PE_init_platform().  The
static personalities were published from the second one, into a catalogue
that the first one had already read.  So the lockdown sweep saw only the
donor's personalities, the platform driver was never matched, no driver
attached, the CPU count was never published -- and the boot thread waits
for that count in ml_wait_max_cpus(), for ever.

So the publication moves earlier: it happens from iokit_post_constructor_init,
right after the root nub is attached and long before the lockdown.  The
sweep that comes after the lockdown still finds them there, so it is
published once and the second sweep reads the same catalogue.
